# EEST cases that yevm fails and that evm2, reth's own EVM, fails too. tests/eest.rs
# does not count them as failures; it fails if one of them starts passing, so the list stays
# exact. One `<fixture file>::<case name>` per line, as in tmp/eest/report-<evm>.txt.
#
# All 14 are EIP-7610 creation collisions: a CREATE, CREATE2 or creation transaction targets
# an address that has storage but no code and nonce 0. The spec makes the creation fail and
# consume all its gas. The database interface both EVMs read state through (evm2's `Database`,
# as reth uses it) cannot tell whether an account has storage, so evm2 and yevm detect a
# collision from code and nonce only and deploy the contract. reth's and revm's own EF test
# runners skip these files for that reason. On mainnet, reaching such an address takes a hash
# collision.
# Checked on 2026-11-13 with EEST v5.4.0 develop: `EEST_EVM=evm2` fails exactly these cases, with
# the same errors (tmp/eest/report-yevm.txt and report-evm2.txt are identical). In particular,
# both give the new contract empty storage, so where the init code clears a slot the colliding
# address already holds, neither reads the stale value.
